From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Maria Blasco <josep.maria.blasco@epbcn.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 11:46:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] WebAssembly port: build and base runtime

Build ooRexx for WebAssembly with Emscripten 6.0.9 (wasm/build-wasm.sh,
cmake/wasm-emscripten-6.0.9-cache.cmake).  Everything is under
if (EMSCRIPTEN) / #if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__); native builds are unchanged.

- static librexx (linked --whole-archive so the _rexx_init() constructor
  that creates the interpreter locks is kept) and librexxapi;
- the interpreter runs on a pthread (PROXY_TO_PTHREAD, pool of 4 workers),
  no Asyncify, native WebAssembly exceptions in the standardized encoding
  (exnref: Chrome 137, Firefox 131, Safari 18.4, Node 22);
- deep recursion ends in Error 11: Activity::checkStackSpace() also probes
  the JS engine's native stack every few activation levels (and the
  expression parser every few nesting levels), with a call that recurses
  through wasm frames, calibrated on each thread to a quarter of its stack;
- the wall clock with sub-millisecond resolution (performance.timeOrigin +
  performance.now(); Emscripten's gettimeofday is Date.now(), whole ms);
- the API server (queues, registrations, macrospace) linked in and reached
  in-process (SysLoopbackConnection);
- rxsock, rxregexp, rxmath, hostemu and rxunixsys embedded in the
  interpreter (PackageManager::embeddedPackages; no dlopen);
- getpwnam()/getpwuid() wrapped to return the user the process runs as
  (Emscripten has no passwd database): the host user under Node, the
  synthetic user "wasm" in the browser;
- rxsock over Emscripten's WebSocket socket emulation, with blocking
  connect/recv/select semantics restored by polling;
- wasm/tests/qualify-node.sh: Node qualification with assertions.

Based on Tom Dyer's (Alchemy) dev1 WebAssembly port, contributed under the
Common Public License 1.0.
